ook><name>OYAMA, NOBORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TATSUMA, TETSU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, YOSHIHITO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HABA MASANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATOZAKI OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAKIZAKI KAORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OYAMA NOBORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TATSUMA TETSU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE YOSHIHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HABA, MASANORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATOZAKI, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAKIZAKI, KAORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OYAMA, NOBORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TATSUMA, TETSU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, YOSHIHITO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A QCM sensor for detecting and measuring the components of a sample from a change in the main resonance frequency or from a change in the impedance caused when the surfaces of electrodes of a sensor device having electrodes opposed to each other on the front and back surfaces of a quartz substrate are exposed to a sample gas or to a sample solution. The sensor device has a multi-channel structure having four opposed electrodes (11A to 14A, 12B to 14B) arranged on the front and back surfaces of a quartz substrate (10). To the electrodes are secured receptors which are different for the components of a sample that is to be detected and measured. Components of a sample are detected and measured at one time using the different electrodes.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un capteur QCM destiné à détecter et à mesurer les composants d'un échantillon sur la base des changements dans la fréquence de résonance principale ou dans l'impédance, ces changements étant survenus lorsque les surfaces des électrodes d'un dispositif de détection possédant des électrodes opposées aux surfaces avant et arrière d'un substrat de quartz sont exposées à un échantillon sous forme de gaz ou de solution.e dispositif de détection possède une structure à canaux multiples et comporte quatre électrodes opposées (de 11 A à 14 B, de 12 B à 14 B) aménagées sur les surfaces avant et arrière d'un substrat de quartz (10). Des récepteurs sont fixés aux électrodes; ils sont différents pour les composants d'un échantillon détecté et mesuré. Les composants d'un échantillon sont détectés et mesurés en une fois au moyen des différentes électrodes.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>